Segment Insights & Market Breakdown
By Type
Hollow Fibre Membrane Oxygenators dominate the market, driven by their high gas exchange efficiency and low priming volumes. Their widespread integration into modern life-support and bypass systems reinforces their leading role.
By Application
The Respiratory segment leads due to the rising use of ECMO in ARDS and acute respiratory failure. Long-term ECMO support, especially in ICUs, continues to expand global utilization.
By End User
Hospitals remain the primary end users, supported by large case volumes, robust infrastructure, and specialized surgical teams.
By Membrane Material
Polymethylpentene (PMP) holds the largest share, driven by its superior performance in long-duration ECMO therapy.
By Level of Care
The Adult segment dominates due to higher prevalence of cardiopulmonary diseases, while Pediatric & Neonatal care remains a crucial innovation-driven niche.
